            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Arabic for to cry, then the Arabic for to dance."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: تعلم",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تعلم — taʿallama — \"to learn (he learned)\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تعلم (taʿallama) is built on the native Arabic root ʿ-l-m, \"to know\" (Lane). Taʿallama is Form V, \"to get oneself taught\", to learn."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
